==Powers and Abilities==
<gallery type="slideshow">
CIU (537).png|Webbing Generation/Wall Scaling
SH (2).png|Web Swinging/Enhanced Speed
CIU (540).png|Web Ensnarement
WALGMO (459).png|Web Slingshot
HT (71).png|Web Net
TT (285).png|Enhanced Strength
The More Things Change, Part 1 (240).png|Enhanced Durability
CIU (534).png|Enhanced Jumping/Enhanced Reflexes
FG (225).png|Enhanced Acrobatics
The More Things Change, Part 1 (247).png|Enhanced Speed/Enhanced Agility
VoV2 (186).png|Web Scaling
AF (107).png|Prehensile Tail/Prehensile Feet
Malefactor (101).png|Bipedalism
</gallery>
Spidermonkey has the ability to expel webbing using a silk as strong as steel cable from his tail,{{Refn|[https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/ben10/images/3/38/AF_Mini_Bible.pdf Alien Force Series Mini Bible]|group = AF Mini Bible|name = bible}} at a distance of over 20 feet.{{Refn|[[:File:Spidermonkey Alien Creation Card.png]]|group=Bandai|name=card2}} His webbing is very sticky, meaning he can use it to trap opponents or blind them by shooting webbing in their face, but it does not stick to him due to a special oil in his fur.{{Refn|group=Bandai|name=card2}} Spidermonkey can also shape his webs into slings to swing across vast distances.<ref>''[[Singlehanded]]''</ref><ref name="ATTWN">''[[And Then There Were None]]''</ref> Spidermonkey uses a sound-based radar system for aiming and firing his webbing.{{Refn|group=Bandai|name=card2}}

Spidermonkey can use his webbing to create web constructs, such as a web slingshot,<ref name="WALGMO">''[[What Are Little Girls Made Of?]]''</ref> and a web net.<ref name="HT">''[[Hero Time]]''</ref>

Spidermonkey has enhanced strength, as he was capable of using a lamp post to hit [[Ultimate Kevin]] up a few feet,<ref name="APP2">''[[Absolute Power: Part 2]]''</ref> carry [[Voratia Rumbletum|Queen Voratia Rumbletum]] over his back,<ref>''[[Tummy Trouble]]''</ref> and carry [[Ben Tennyson (No Watch Timeline)|No Watch Ben]] while web-slinging without any difficulty.<ref name="ATTWN" />

Spidermonkey is very durable considering his size, as shown when he was able to survive seemingly unharmed after several large pieces of concrete fell on him.<ref name="VoVP2">''[[Vengeance of Vilgax: Part 2]]''</ref><ref name="TMTCP1" />

Spidermonkey can jump high in the air and has enhanced reflexes, as shown when he avoided [[Thunderpig]]'s energy flail.<ref>''[[Cough It Up]]''</ref>

Spidermonkey has enhanced agility and enhanced acrobatic skills.<ref name="FG">''[[Fool's Gold]]''</ref>

Spidermonkey has hearing superior to a [[Human (Classic)|human]]'s, as [[Simian]] could hear [[Gwen Tennyson (Classic)|Gwen]] and [[Kevin Levin (Classic)|Kevin]] talking about him from several feet away.<ref name="BoaF" />

Spidermonkey's fingers can stick to and be used to scale vertical surfaces like a spider.{{Refn|group = AF Mini Bible|name = bible}}

Spidermonkey's feet and tail are both prehensile, enabling him to hold and carry multiple objects as if they are extra hands.<ref>''[[Andreas' Fault]]''</ref>

Spidermonkey can assume a bipedal stance for short periods of time, as shown when he stood on two legs after hitting Ultimate Kevin.<ref name="APP2" />

==Weaknesses==
<gallery type="slideshow">
Fame (454).png|Exploitable Webbing
GCBC (460).png|Dissolvable Webs
BB (156).png|Trapped in Webbing
Simple (183).png|Affected by Sleeping Gas
</gallery>
Spidermonkey can get tangled by his own webs.<ref name="WALGMO" /> <ref>''[[Busy Box]]''</ref> Furthermore, enemies can easily use his webs to their advantage.<ref>''[[Fame]]''</ref>

Spidermonkey's webs can be frozen and made brittle by the ice breath of a [[Polar Manzardill]].<ref>''[[Collect This]]''</ref> They can also be dissolved by heat generated by a [[Crystalsapien (Classic)|Crystalsapien]].<ref>''[[Good Copy, Bad Copy]]''</ref>

Being an [[Arachnachimp (Classic)|Arachnachimp]], Spidermonkey is a target to all the predatory species of [[Aranhascimmia]], such as [[Root Shark|Root Sharks]].<ref name="SS" />

Spidermonkey is vulnerable to electricity, as demonstrated with [[Simian]].<ref name="BoaF" /><ref name="SS" />

Spidermonkey can be rendered unconscious if hit by a sedative quill from a member of [[Argit]]'s [[Argit's Species|species]], as demonstrated with Simian.<ref>''[[The Color of Monkey]]''</ref>

Spidermonkey is vulnerable to toxic gases.<ref>''[[Simple]]''</ref>

==History==
===Alien Force===
*Spidermonkey first appeared in ''[[Be-Knighted]]'', where he replaced the [[Mapmaker]]'s broken [[Universal Translator]] with a new one.
*In ''[[What Are Little Girls Made Of?]]'', Spidermonkey was defeated by [[Verdona]].
*In ''[[Darkstar Rising]]'', Spidermonkey briefly fought [[Michael Morningstar (Classic)|Darkstar]] before switching into [[Jetray (Classic)|Jetray]].
*In ''[[Good Copy, Bad Copy]]'', [[Albedo|Negative]] Spidermonkey defeated Jetray and was about to fight [[Chromastone (Classic)|Chromastone]] before the latter ended up reverting.
*In ''[[Birds of a Feather]]'', Spidermonkey battled some [[DNAlien]]s and was saved by [[Simian]].
*In ''[[Vengeance of Vilgax: Part 2]]'', Spidermonkey escaped the Omnitrix and battled [[Brainstorm]] before getting recaptured.
*In ''[[Inferno]]'', Spidermonkey fought [[Vulkanus]] before switching into Jetray to stop a bomb from exploding, even though he tried to turn into [[Humungousaur (Classic)|Humungousaur]] in order to catch the bomb.
*In ''[[Simple]]'', Spidermonkey tried to stop the Blue Team, but failed and was captured by them for execution before being rescued by [[Gwen Tennyson (Classic)|Gwen]] and [[Probity]].
*In ''[[Fool's Gold]]'', Spidermonkey stopped some [[Decka's Species|aliens]] from causing trouble in [[Walton]].
*In ''[[Singlehanded]]'', Spidermonkey fought and tried to escape from [[Sunder]], but was eventually trapped by him, so he switched into [[Humungousaur (Classic)|Humungousaur]].
*In ''[[If All Else Fails]]'', Spidermonkey battled a [[Highbreed]].
*In ''[[Busy Box]]'', Spidermonkey was defeated by the [[Naljian Destructor]].
*In ''[[The Final Battle: Part 1]]'', Negative Spidermonkey failed to capture [[Max Tennyson (Classic)|Max]].
*In ''[[The Final Battle: Part 2]]'', Spidermonkey was briefly used by [[Vilgax (Classic)|Vilgax]]'s [[Bioid]]s.

===Ultimate Alien===  
*In ''[[Fame]]'', Spidermonkey was seen on TV. Later, Spidermonkey fought [[Bivalvan]] before going [[Ultimate Spidermonkey|Ultimate]]. Spidermonkey appeared again when he was changing back to [[Ben Tennyson (Classic)|Ben]].
*In ''[[Video Games (Episode)|Video Games]]'', Spidermonkey failed to defeat the [[Stalker]], so he tried to switched into [[Chromastone (Classic)|Chromastone]] but switched into [[Swampfire]] instead.
*In ''[[Andreas' Fault]]'', Spidermonkey battled some [[Forever Knights]] in [[Mr. Smoothy (Classic)|Mr. Smoothy]].
*In ''[[Hero Time]]'', Spidermonkey saved [[Jennifer Nocturne]] from some criminals.
*In ''[[Reflected Glory]]'', Spidermonkey fought [[Psyphon]] before going Ultimate.
*In ''[[Perplexahedron (Episode)|Perplexahedron]]'', Spidermonkey escaped an acid room in the [[Perplexahedron]] with [[Kevin Levin (Classic)|Kevin]].
*In ''[[Absolute Power: Part 2]]'', Spidermonkey was defeated by [[Ultimate Kevin]].
*In ''[[The Transmogrification of Eunice]]'', Spidermonkey battled [[Sunder]] before going Ultimate. Spidermonkey appeared again later when he was changing back to Ben.
*In ''[[Ben 10,000 Returns]]'' Spidermonkey fought some of [[Eon]]'s [[Eon's Minions|minions]].
*In ''[[It's Not Easy Being Gwen]]'', Spidermonkey met up with [[Gwen Tennyson (Classic)|Gwen]].
*In ''[[Simian Says]]'', Spidermonkey fought [[Mizaru]] before going Ultimate. Spidermonkey appeared again later when he was changing back to Ben.
*In ''[[The Purge]]'', Spidermonkey went Ultimate to battle [[Sir Driscoll]].
*In ''[[Double or Nothing]]'', Spidermonkey went Ultimate to battle [[Hugh]]. Later, he went Ultimate to battle [[Albedo]].
*In ''[[The Perfect Girlfriend]]'', Spidermonkey tried to fix an elevator and was saved by "[[Elena Valadis|Julie]]" when it nearly fell on him.
*In ''[[The Mother of All Vreedles]]'', Spidermonkey went to battle the [[Vreedle Brothers]], [[Ma Vreedle]] and [[Dodecahedron Vreedle|Dodecahedron]] before going Ultimate. Spidermonkey appeared again later when he was changing back to Ben.
*In ''[[Ben 10-Generator Rex: Heroes United|Ben 10/Generator Rex: Heroes United]]'', Spidermonkey appeared as one of the many aliens when [[Ben Tennyson (Classic)|Ben]] was explaining his story to [[Rex Salazar (Generator Rex)|Rex]].

===Omniverse=== 
*In ''[[The More Things Change: Part 1]]'', Spidermonkey fought [[Crabdozer (Transformation)|Crabdozer]].
*In ''[[So Long, and Thanks for All the Smoothies]]'', Spidermonkey defeated two [[Incursean (Classic)|Incursean]] soldiers.
*In ''[[Have I Got a Deal for You]]'', Spidermonkey and [[Pax]] snuck into [[Blarney T. Hokestar|Professor Hokestar]]'s [[Extraterrestrial Emporium]] and found a [[Screegit]].
*In ''[[Malefactor]]'', a kid demanded that [[Ben Tennyson (Classic)|Ben]] turned into Spidermonkey so he could dunk him in the Dunk Ben 10 game.
*In ''[[Tummy Trouble]]'', Spidermonkey carried [[Voratia Rumbletum|Queen Rumbletum]] to safety and battled [[Attea|General Attea]].
*In ''[[Store 23]]'', Spidermonkey was one of several aliens [[Ben Tennyson (Classic)|Ben Prime]] was showcasing for [[Ben 23]].
*In ''[[And Then There Were None]]'', Spidermonkey saved [[Ben Tennyson (No Watch Timeline)|No Watch Ben]] from the evil Bens and travelled to the latter's [[No Watch Timeline|version]] of [[Los Soledad]] with him so they could meet up with [[Professor Paradox]]. Negative Spidermonkey briefly appeared before going Ultimate.
*In ''[[Cough It Up]]'', Spidermonkey battled [[Thunderpig]] and [[EightEight]].
*In ''[[Malgax Attacks]]'', Negative Spidermonkey briefly appeared before going Ultimate.
*In ''[[A New Dawn]]'', Spidermonkey appeared for a short time when Ben was cycling through his aliens.

===[[Time Heals Timeline]]===
*In ''[[Time Heals]]'', Spidermonkey was found by the Prime Timeline Gwen in [[Hex (Classic)|Hex]]'s torture chamber.

===[[Ultimate Alien Future Timeline|Ultimate Alien Future]]=== 
*In ''[[Ben 10,000 Returns]]'', [[Ultimate Ben]] used Spidermonkey's agility to battle some of [[Eon's Minions|Eon's minions]] on the [[Rustbucket 3]].

